  {
   "id": "hilum",
   "label": "Hilar margins (bile duct, portal vein, hepatic artery)",
   "type": "select",
   "group": "Macroscopy",
   "options": [
    "Submitted en face",
    "Not submitted"
   ],
   "default": "Submitted en face",
   "reference": {
    "title": "Explant grossing checklist",
    "intro": "Sample the hilum before slicing, slice thinly, and map every nodule to a segment and to the imaging (RCPath G050; UCLA total hepatectomy grossing protocol).",
    "columns": 2,
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Identify and measure",
      "points": [
       "Segments 1 to 8; weigh after opening the gallbladder and rinsing out the bile, and give three dimensions (RCPath G050)",
       "Describe adherent structures such as diaphragm (UCLA)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Hilum before slicing",
      "points": [
       "One cassette en face with the portal vein, hepatic artery and common hepatic duct margins; one with the hepatic vein margins, inked differentially (UCLA)",
       "Thrombus in the portal vein, hepatic artery or hepatic veins: colour, size and site (UCLA)",
       "Involvement of the main left or right portal vein or of the three main hepatic veins, with the vessel diameter (RCPath G050)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Gallbladder and nodes",
      "points": [
       "Gallbladder size, contents, mucosa and stones; cystic duct shave and neck, body and fundus sections (UCLA)",
       "Sampling a macroscopically normal gallbladder is optional (RCPath G050)",
       "Submit hilar nodes entirely (UCLA)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Slice",
      "points": [
       "Horizontal slices at right angles, for imaging correlation, as thin as possible and no more than 10 mm (RCPath G050)",
       "Slices of 5 mm are advised, because thicker slices miss small lesions (Int J Organ Transplant Med 2017)",
       "Background: normal, bile-stained, nutmeg, or fibrotic or cirrhotic (RCPath G050)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Map every nodule",
      "points": [
       "Number each mass or prominent nodule: segment, size, description, distance from the capsule, necrosis with the viable dimension, and vascular invasion (UCLA)",
       "Many nodules: full detail for the five largest, and the size range and location of the rest (CAP HCC protocol 4.2.0.0)",
       "Not every imaging lesion found: the pathologist sees the specimen and the gross description says so (UCLA)",
       "No tumour and no lesion: serial slicing shows no mass or prominent nodule (UCLA)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Sample",
      "points": [
       "At least three tumour blocks, with all macroscopically distinct areas (RCPath G050)",
       "After treatment, a tumour of 20 mm or less entirely through its largest diameter, plus one section for each further 10 mm (RCPath G050; CAP)",
       "Any nodule appreciably larger than the background (CAP) or differing in colour, texture or appearance (Int J Hepatol 2016)",
       "Four background blocks, right and left lobe, central and peripheral (UCLA), one of them as far from the tumour as possible (RCPath G050)"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
